body:
Implements all remaining DX Phase 2 items from `DX_ROADMAP.md`: custom error map, "Did you mean?" suggestions, pretty-print formatter, branded types, and strict cross-reference validation for `defineStack()`.

### Branded Types (`shared/branded-types.zod.ts`)
- `ObjectName`, `FieldName`, `ViewName`, `AppName`, `FlowName`, `RoleName` — Zod `.brand()` types for compile-time identifier safety

### "Did you mean?" Suggestions (`shared/suggestions.zod.ts`)
- Space-optimized Levenshtein distance + fuzzy matching
- 40+ alias mappings for common FieldType typos (`string`→`text`, `dropdown`→`select`, `int`→`number`, etc.)

### Custom Zod v4 Error Map (`shared/error-map.zod.ts`)
- `objectStackErrorMap` — contextual error messages for `invalid_value`, `too_small`, `too_big`, `invalid_type`, `invalid_format`, `unrecognized_keys`
- `formatZodError()` / `formatZodIssue()` — CLI-friendly pretty-print
- `safeParsePretty()` — parse + format in one call

```ts
const result = safeParsePretty(ObjectStackDefinitionSchema, config, 'objectstack.config.ts');
if (!result.success) {
  console.error(result.formatted);
  // objectstack.config.ts (2 issues):
  //   ✗ objects.0.fields.status.type: Invalid field type 'dropdown'. Did you mean 'select'?
  //   ✗ manifest.name: Required property 'name' is missing.
}
```

### Strict `defineStack()` (`stack.zod.ts`)
- `defineStack(config, { strict: true })` validates cross-references: workflows (`objectName`), approvals (`object`), hooks (`object`), and view data sources against defined objects

```ts
defineStack({
  manifest: { id: 'com.acme.crm', name: 'crm', version: '1.0.0', type: 'app' },
  objects: [{ name: 'lead', fields: { status: { type: 'text' } } }],
  workflows: [{ name: 'qualify', objectName: 'nonexistent', triggerType: 'on_create' }],
}, { strict: true });
// throws: "Workflow 'qualify' references object 'nonexistent' which is not defined in objects."
```

### Test coverage
65 new tests across 3 new test files + expanded `stack.test.ts` (194 files, 5243 tests total).

